{"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "intatomic", "ucas": "w(acc: f32, i: u32 in 0..255) = atomic_add_shared(acc, f32(i) * 0.25)\nintatomic w", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "intatomic", "model": "gt1030", "scope": "shared", "cost_float": 24.25, "rewritten": true, "atomic": "atomic_add_shared(acc, i32(i))", "scale_log2": 2, "cost": 6.625, "defined": "w_ia"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "derivation", "text": "the addend's binary grid and magnitude from its structure and ranges; the sum fits 32 bits"}, "files": [], "text": "intatomic w under gt1030: a shared float atomic add of 0.25f32(i), at most 1024 into one cell\n  the float add costs 24.25, an integer one 6.625\n  the addend is k 2^-2 with |k| <= 255, exactly: every leaf is an integer or a binary constant, the\n  operations keep the grid, and no f32 value on the way needs more than 24 bits, so none rounds\n  the sum of 1024 of them is at most 261120 2^-2: it fits 32 bits (261120 < 2^31), so the integer sum is the exact sum\n  the float sum would be exact too (it stays within 24 bits): the two agree bit for bit, in every order\n  the integer addend: i32(i)\n  -> atomic_add_shared(acc, i32(i)): addend and atomic cost 6.625 against 28.25 (-76.5%)\n     the cell is an i32 holding the sum times 2^2; every other access of it changes too: a store of v\n     stores i32(v * 2^2), a read is f32(cell) * 2^-2 (a conversion and a multiply: 4 a read)\n  defined w_ia: the atomic's old value read back as a float\n"}
{"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "intatomic", "ucas": "intatomic w count 100000000", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "intatomic", "model": "gt1030", "scope": "shared", "cost_float": 24.25, "rewritten": false}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "intatomic w under gt1030: a shared float atomic add of 0.25f32(i), at most 100000000 into one cell\n  the float add costs 24.25, an integer one 6.625\n  the addend is k 2^-2 with |k| <= 255, exactly: every leaf is an integer or a binary constant, the\n  operations keep the grid, and no f32 value on the way needs more than 24 bits, so none rounds\n  -> not rewritten: 100000000 addends of up to 255 can reach 25500000000, past 2^31 - 1; fewer adds (`count N`) or a narrower range\n"}
