{"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "banks", "ucas": "banks row, col size 1024", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "banks", "model": "gt1030", "accesses": [{"index": "32r + lane", "degree": 1, "exact": true, "price": 3}, {"index": "32lane + c", "degree": 32, "exact": true, "price": 127}], "price": 130, "swizzle": "i + (i >> 5)", "price_after": 10, "rewritten_accesses": [{"defined": "row_sw", "index": "t1 + (t1 >> 5) where t1 = 32r + lane", "degree": 1}, {"defined": "col_sw", "index": "t1 + (t1 >> 5) where t1 = 32lane + c", "degree": 1}], "rewritten": true}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "the swizzle keeps the indices apart; the degrees are enumerated over every warp"}, "files": [], "text": "banks under gt1030: 32 banks of 4 bytes, a warp of 32 lanes, 4-byte elements; a shared load 3, each further address on a bank +4\n  row = 32r + lane\n    lane parameter lane; conflict degree 1: index = 1 lane + b: two lanes share a bank when 32 divides 1 (l - l'), that is when 32 divides l - l', so 32 gcd(1, 32) / 32 = 1 lane a bank; all 32 cases enumerated too\n    price 3\n  col = 32lane + c\n    lane parameter lane; conflict degree 32: index = 32 lane + b: two lanes share a bank when 32 divides 32 (l - l'), that is when 1 divides l - l', so 32 gcd(32, 32) / 32 = 32 lanes a bank; all 32 cases enumerated too\n    price 127\n  -> swizzle every index i of the array: i + (i >> 5)\n     it is strictly increasing (i + 1 lands after i), so no two indices meet; the array grows to 1055 elements: every index enumerated\n     row_sw = t1 + (t1 >> 5) where t1 = 32r + lane\n       conflict degree 1 (index = 1 lane + b: two lanes share a bank when 32 divides 1 (l - l'), that is when 32 divides l - l', so 32 gcd(1, 32) / 32 = 1 lane a bank; all 32 cases enumerated too): price 3 + 2 for the swizzle\n     col_sw = t1 + (t1 >> 5) where t1 = 32lane + c\n       conflict degree 1 (index = 33 lane + b: two lanes share a bank when 32 divides 33 (l - l'), that is when 32 divides l - l', so 32 gcd(33, 32) / 32 = 1 lane a bank; all 32 cases enumerated too): price 3 + 2 for the swizzle\n     total 10 against 130 (-92.3%); every access of the array takes the swizzle, reads and writes alike\n"}
