{"id": 9, "ok": true, "cmd": "spirv_simplify", "ucas": "use addy; spvsimplify nofile", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "banks", "model": "addy", "accesses": [{"index": "(v79 << 5) + lane", "degree": 1, "exact": true, "price": 3}, {"index": "(lane << 5) + v80", "degree": 32, "exact": true, "price": 127}], "price": 130, "swizzle": "i xor (i >> 5 & 31)", "price_after": 12, "rewritten_accesses": [{"defined": "_sh_1_sw", "index": "t1 xor t1 >> 5 & 0x1f where t1 = (v79 << 5) + lane", "degree": 1}, {"defined": "_sh_2_sw", "index": "t1 xor t1 >> 5 & 0x1f where t1 = (lane << 5) + v80", "degree": 1}], "rewritten": true}, "results": [{"kind": "spirv_simplify", "instructions": 105, "dead_removed": 0, "model": "addy", "cost_before": 23, "cost_after": 19, "cost_driver_baseline": 19, "driver_trivial_count": 2, "driver_trivial_gain": 4, "assumptions": [], "rewrites": [{"from": "%32 = OpIMul %uint %79 %uint_32", "to": "OpShiftLeftLogical %uint %79 %ucas_uint_5", "why": "a multiply by a power of two is a shift", "gain": 2, "line": 8, "proof": "sat", "driver_trivial": true}, {"from": "%65 = OpIMul %uint %16 %uint_32", "to": "OpShiftLeftLogical %uint %16 %ucas_uint_5", "why": "a multiply by a power of two is a shift", "gain": 2, "line": 12, "proof": "sat", "driver_trivial": true}]}, {"kind": "banks", "model": "addy", "accesses": [{"index": "(v79 << 5) + lane", "degree": 1, "exact": true, "price": 3}, {"index": "(lane << 5) + v80", "degree": 32, "exact": true, "price": 127}], "price": 130, "swizzle": "i xor (i >> 5 & 31)", "price_after": 12, "rewritten_accesses": [{"defined": "_sh_1_sw", "index": "t1 xor t1 >> 5 & 0x1f where t1 = (v79 << 5) + lane", "degree": 1}, {"defined": "_sh_2_sw", "index": "t1 xor t1 >> 5 & 0x1f where t1 = (lane << 5) + v80", "degree": 1}], "rewritten": true}], "notes": [{"kind": "info", "text": "the code was compiled to SPIR-V with glslangValidator"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "the swizzle keeps the indices apart; the degrees are enumerated over every warp"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: the code was compiled to SPIR-V with glslangValidator\n  optimized with spirv-opt -O (what follows is beyond that)\ncost model: addy\nsimplify: 105 SPIR-V instructions, 2 rewrites proved by SAT (bit-precise: equal for every input), 0 dead instructions removed\n  integer arithmetic cost under addy (each instruction once), beyond what spirv-opt -O and a driver's back end do: 19 -> 19 (+0.0%)\n  counting the strength reductions any driver also does: 23 -> 19 (-17.4%)\n  also done by any driver compiler (2 rewrites, -4; kept in the written module, not counted above): 2 a multiply by a power of two is a shift\n  beyond those, no cheaper form of an integer instruction could be proved\n  proved; the operands' definitions were expanded up to 16 levels, the rest (loads, loop phis, spec constants) are free inputs\nmemory under addy:\n  workgroup array sh (1024 elements of 4 bytes, 2 accesses):\nbanks under addy: 32 banks of 4 bytes, a warp of 32 lanes, 4-byte elements; a shared load 3, each further address on a bank +4\n  _sh_1 = (v79 << 5) + lane\n    lane parameter lane; conflict degree 1: index = 1 lane + b: two lanes share a bank when 32 divides 1 (l - l'), that is when 32 divides l - l', so 32 gcd(1, 32) / 32 = 1 lane a bank; all 32 cases enumerated too\n    price 3\n  _sh_2 = (lane << 5) + v80\n    lane parameter lane; conflict degree 32: index = 32 lane + b: two lanes share a bank when 32 divides 32 (l - l'), that is when 1 divides l - l', so 32 gcd(32, 32) / 32 = 32 lanes a bank; all 32 cases enumerated too\n    price 127\n  -> swizzle every index i of the array: i xor (i >> 5 & 31)\n     applied twice it gives i back (the row i >> 5 is not changed by it), so it is a bijection of [0, 1024): every index enumerated\n     _sh_1_sw = t1 xor t1 >> 5 & 0x1f where t1 = (v79 << 5) + lane\n       conflict degree 1 (every warp and every value of the uniform parameters enumerated: 32 cases): price 3 + 3 for the swizzle\n     _sh_2_sw = t1 xor t1 >> 5 & 0x1f where t1 = (lane << 5) + v80\n       conflict degree 1 (every warp and every value of the uniform parameters enumerated: 32 cases): price 3 + 3 for the swizzle\n     total 12 against 130 (-90.8%); every access of the array takes the swizzle, reads and writes alike\n    written into the module: the 2 access chains of the array index it through the swizzle\n  spirv-val accepts the written module\n  (nofile: simplified.spvasm, 3703 bytes, checksum d2dd484d)\n"}
